{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cc714ea573ced272cbeb576a988e9871a9849c3b98bf7c627101d0958b54c72f","digest":{"component_or_area":"review bot retrigger","key_entities":["retrigger.py","TRIGGER_TOKEN","_TOKEN_RE","_RETIRED_TOKEN_RE","rerun-llm-review","recheck-review","gerrit_to_platform.ini.template","post_comment","_ACCEPTED_MESSAGE","_refusal_message","app.py","reconcile.py","test_review_bot_retrigger.py"],"problem_keywords":["trigger collision","CI dispatch","substring matching","retired trigger word","review bot"],"propositions":["The LLM re-review trigger word 'recheck-review' collides with the external CI ChatOps substring matcher, causing the Verified workflow to dispatch when the retired word appears in comments.","All bot reply texts must be scrubbed of mapped trigger words to prevent the bot's own Gerrit comments from re-dispatching CI.","A hard cutover to 'rerun-llm-review' eliminates the collision by choosing a token that shares no substring with any mapping key in the ini template.","Comments carrying the retired word must post a refusal reply and never enqueue a review or reset a vote.","The retired word must survive only in retrigger.py detector and its test module, with all other occurrences updated to the new trigger in docs and codebase."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787887938145162001,"uuid":"6582558a-a2d1-46d8-a6c6-f9ceb7dea957"}